---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import GuideArticle from '../../components/v2/templates/GuideArticle.astro';
import FAQ from '../../components/FAQ.astro';
import { siteImages } from '../../data/images';
import { getPageSEO } from '../../utils/seo';

const faqItems = [
  { question: 'What should I review in the shop?', answer: 'Read the current shop information and compare it with the materials and restaurant categories you need.' },
  { question: 'Does the Wiki list a fixed shop schedule?', answer: 'No. Use the information currently shown in the game rather than assuming a universal schedule.' },
  { question: 'Where can I review ingredient entries?', answer: 'Use the Ingredients Hub for the directory and individual ingredient pages.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout pageId="guides-shop-restock" breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Guides', href: '/guides/' }, { label: getPageSEO('guides-shop-restock').h1 }]}>
<GuideArticle
  title={getPageSEO('guides-shop-restock').h1}
  kicker="Resource management guide"
  intro="Check the stock shown in your current server and avoid relying on an unverified universal restock timer."
  tableOfContents
  heroImage={siteImages.ingredientsHero}
  relatedLinks={[
    { label: 'Grocery', href: '/grocery/', description: 'Review the Grocery and its connection with ingredients.' },
    { label: 'Ingredients', href: '/ingredients/', description: 'Browse the Ingredient directory and entity pages.' },
    { label: 'Recipes', href: '/recipes/', description: 'Learn how ingredients connect with cooking and food.' },
    { label: 'Equipment', href: '/equipment/', description: 'Browse restaurant tools and cooking equipment.' },
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="direct-answer">Direct Answer</h2>
  <p>Public gameplay shows shop listings and unavailable stock, but the material reviewed does not establish one universal restock interval or whether refresh state is global, server-specific, or player-specific. Treat the current shop display as authoritative.</p>

  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>The Shop and Grocery interfaces organize items used by the restaurant. Their visible categories, stock, quantities, and timing can be version-sensitive, so this guide explains how to check the live state instead of publishing a permanent schedule.</p>

  <h2 id="how-it-works">What Is Confirmed</h2>
  <p>Dated gameplay captures show item listings with stock information and cases where an item is unavailable. They do not prove a fixed refresh interval. Review the restaurant first, then read the current Shop or Grocery interface and use the matching Wiki category for context.</p>

  <h2 id="resource-planning-process">Resource Planning Process</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Review the ingredients and restaurant areas currently in use.</li>
    <li>Identify the material or category that needs attention.</li>
    <li>Open the current shop interface.</li>
    <li>Read the available labels and item information.</li>
    <li>Use the related Wiki Hub for additional context.</li>
    <li>Return to the restaurant workflow and review the next need.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="gameplay-tips">Gameplay Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Review ingredient information before it interrupts preparation.</li>
    <li>Use the Recipes and Food pages to understand the wider cooking workflow.</li>
    <li>Keep optional customization separate from immediate restaurant needs.</li>
    <li>Rely on the current interface when shop information changes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="common-mistakes">Restock Troubleshooting</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Following an old shop list without checking the current interface.</li>
    <li>Reviewing materials without connecting them to restaurant needs.</li>
    <li>Changing several restaurant categories before observing the workflow.</li>
    <li>Assuming every server or update presents the same information.</li>
  </ul>

  <FAQ slot="faq" items={faqItems} />
</GuideArticle>
</BaseLayout>
